    "created_at": "2020-11-25T17:41:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-25T17:46:15Z",
    "body": "All the official init scripts do something like `export STARSHIP_SHELL=shell-name`, ideally any nushell starship init script would set the `STARSHIP_SHELL` variable to for example `nu`. The `bash` and `zsh` values cause the prompt to become mangled on other shells.\r\nI remember some talk about having `starship init` autodetect the shell, so detecting nu from the starship side might also be possible.\r\n\r\nSee also similiar problems #1115 #1856",
